# API Backwards Compatibility Rule

## NEVER remove or rename an API endpoint that a mobile app binary uses.

Mobile app binaries are frozen at submission time. Unlike the web app, 
you cannot update them instantly. Any endpoint change breaks existing 
users until they update.

When changing an API endpoint:
1. Keep the OLD endpoint working as a thin shim/redirect
2. Add the NEW endpoint with the improved interface  
3. Both must work simultaneously
4. Comment the old endpoint with: # COMPAT: kept for iOS build <= X.Y.Z
5. Only remove old endpoints after 6+ months AND confirming zero traffic

This applies to:
- URL paths (don't rename /api/billing/token-pack/checkout)
- Request body field names (don't rename pack → pack_id)
- Response body field names
- Authentication methods
- Query parameter names

The web app at app.sovereignsanctuary.net can be updated instantly via
`bash scripts/deploy_flutter_web.sh`. iOS/Android cannot.

